## Time Tracking

- **Core rule: Use timeframes appropriate to temporal distance. Track realistic time passage through actions and environment.**
- Under 1 month: Specific (“X days/weeks ago”, exact date)
- Over 1 month: Approximate timeframe allowed (“a few months ago”, “a while back”, “long ago”)
- Exception: Significant events (trauma, anniversaries) or official records → exact dates permitted regardless of distance
- Do not compress long-elapsed time into short-range phrasing; events crossing a year boundary must not be described as “a few months ago.”
- "Yesterday" refers only to one day before today's date shown in the status window. If it is not that date, do not use "yesterday."
</Time_Check>
